    "title": "Selection Sunday: How to watch the women's bracket reveal live tonight ahead of the 2026 NCAA March Madness basketball tournament",
    "text": "It's time for March Madness. Tonight, the brackets for the 2026 NCAA tournament will be revealed. The women’s 68-team bracket reveal will air live on ESPN at 8 p.m. ET. Prior to the women's bracket reveal, the men's will air at 6 p.m. on CBS. Just like last year, the two tournaments are spread across a range of channels, so if you’re looking for how to watch March Madness — in addition to Selection Sunday — Yahoo Sports has you covered. Here’s everything you need to know about watching Selection Sunday for the women’s NCAA tournament live this weekend, plus how to watch March Madness in 2026.Date: Sunday, March 15, 2026AdvertisementTime: 8 p.m. ETTV channel: ESPNStreaming: ESPN Unlimited, DirecTV and moreWhen is Selection Sunday for March Madness?The madness begins on Selection Sunday, March 15, when the Selection Committee reveals the full NCAA tournament bracket for both the men's and women's teams. The women's bracket will be revealed at 8 p.m. ET. The men’s bracket will precede the women's at 6 p.m. ET.Selection Sunday TV channelThe women’s March Madness bracket reveal will air live on ESPN. The men’s bracket reveal will air on CBS.How to watch Selection Sunday live without cableESPN's streaming platform offers thousands of exclusive live events, original studio shows, and acclaimed series that air across ESPN's suite of seven linear channels, as well as exclusive content on ESPN+, ABC on ESPN, SEC+, ACCNX and more. The tier costs $29.99/month or $299.99/year. ESPN Select allows subscribers to access exclusive content only available on the app, and an extensive archive of on-demand content (including the entire 30 For 30 library, select ESPN films, game replays, and more). Whether you purchase a standalone plan, add-on or Disney bundle plan, the service provides access to thousands of sports events for $12.99/month or $129.99/year. DirecTV is currently offering its Choice tier (typically $115+/month with fees) for just $80 (after fees) for the first month. DirecTV's Choice tier gives you access to tons of sports channels, including ESPN, the ACC Network, the Big Ten Network, the SEC Network and plenty of local Regional Sports Networks. Plus, you'll get access to ABC, NBC, CBS and Fox. Whichever package you choose, you'll get unlimited Cloud DVR storage and access to ESPN's new streaming tier, ESPN Unlimited. The best part is that you can currently try all this out for free for 5 days. If you're interested in trying a live TV streaming service for the start of March Madness but aren't ready to commit, we recommend starting with DirecTV. When does March Madness start?Both the men’s and women’s NCAA tournament brackets will be revealed on Sunday, March 15. The men's games then tip off with the First Four on Tuesday, March 17. The women's side will tip off on Wednesday, March 18.AdvertisementWhat channel is March Madness on in 2026?Games in the men’s NCAA tournament will air across CBS, TBS, TNT and TruTV. The women’s NCAA tournament will air across the ESPN suite — ESPN, ESPN2, ESPNU, ESPNews and ABC.-Don’t have cable? Don’t worry. You can stream the men’s games easily with a subscription to Paramount+ Premium and HBO Max Standard, or a liveTV streaming service like DirecTV, Fubo or Sling. The women’s games will be accessible via an ESPN Unlimited subscription (or any live-TV streaming service that includes the ESPN suite).How to watch March Madness 2026:",
